# The build stage copies the source and restores inside the image. Anything a host build left behind
# is either useless there or actively harmful: an obj directory carries absolute paths from the
# machine that wrote it, and restoring over one fails in ways that read as a broken Dockerfile.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/cdk.out/
**/node_modules/
**/TestResults/
**/test-results/

.git/
.github/
.idea/
.vs/
.vscode/

docs/
infra/
tests/
scripts/

# The samples are published from the host, by the commands in the README, against the queue this
# stack exposes. Nothing inside either image reads them.
samples/
